Control: an interface gains a required method and an implementation in
another package is not updated. That breaks the build and needs a person.

=== both package.json
{ "name": "r", "private": true, "workspaces": ["packages/*"] }
=== both packages/store/package.json
{ "name": "@r/store", "private": true, "main": "src/index.ts" }
=== both packages/app/package.json
{ "name": "@r/app", "private": true, "main": "src/index.ts", "dependencies": { "@r/store": "*" } }
=== base packages/store/src/index.ts
export interface Store {
  get(key: string): string;
}
=== head packages/store/src/index.ts
export interface Store {
  get(key: string): string;
  set(key: string, value: string): void;
}
=== both packages/app/src/memory.ts
import type { Store } from '@r/store';

export const memory: Store = {
  get: (key) => key,
};
=== expect
row contract-field-added-required ● title~"`Store` gains a required `set` method" why~"not changed yet" why~"`packages/app/src/memory.ts`"
attention 1
